{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1111412-cobra-style","id":1111412,"title":"Cobra Style","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-04T14:27:06-07:00","id":1111412,"title":"Cobra Style","content":"This was one of my favorite of the late 2E Martial Art styles. Does anyone know if there has been any homebrews to update it to 3E?<br /> <br /> If not, I may give it a shot as my first Ex3 style attempt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1333-wednesday","name":"Wednesday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T16:12:29-07:00","id":1111443,"title":"","content":"I've got an incomplete version of it but the direction I took with it might not be what you want from the style.<br /> <br /> Essentially, my Cobra Style isn't the synergistic style John wrote but a re-imagined poison style where you poison your opponent early into a fight then a lot of its weirder charms are now about preying on their victim's vulnerable mental state. Think of the various boss fights in the Arkham series where Batman is tripping balls and fighting his inner demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T22:18:47-07:00","id":1111557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1111412-cobra-style?p=1111443#post1111443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got an incomplete version of it but the direction I took with it might not be what you want from the style.<br /> <br /> Essentially, my Cobra Style isn't the synergistic style John wrote but a re-imagined poison style where you poison your opponent early into a fight then a lot of its weirder charms are now about preying on their victim's vulnerable mental state. Think of the various boss fights in the Arkham series where Batman is tripping balls and fighting his inner demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what I was looking for exactly, but it would also work. I would like to see it if it's a state you're comfortable putting out there.<br /> <br /> Thanks for responding!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1333-wednesday","name":"Wednesday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T16:13:08-07:00","id":1111869,"title":"","content":"Mostly it lacks the Mastery and Celestial keywords. There's probably other issues too since I started work on it during the playtest.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Cobra Style<br /> <br /> Showing the Cobra\u2019s Fangs<br /> Cost: 3m, Mins: Martial Arts 3, Essence 1; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: One Action<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> Once per scene, the Martial Artist may halve the halve the Hardness of his target but ignores any damage that his attack may inflict in favour of poisoning the target with Serpent\u2019s Venom.<br /> This charm is reset upon successfully crashing an opponent.<br /> <br /> Cobra Eye Splendor<br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Martial Arts 3, Essence 1; Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Showing the Cobra\u2019s Fangs<br /> The Martial Artist uses his expertise of poisons and its effects upon the mind coupled with hypnotic like a snake ready to strike the Martial Artist takes advantage of their opponent\u2019s disadvantages.<br /> In response to an attack the Martial Artist may doubles any poison based penalties that the attacker is suffering from.<br /> <br /> King Cobra Strikes<br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Martial Arts 3, Essence 1; Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Counterattack, Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Showing the Cobra\u2019s Fangs<br /> The Martial Artist makes an unarmed counterattack that is considered to be poisoned with Serpent\u2019s Venom.<br /> <br /> Cobra Form<br /> Cost: 6m, Mins: Martial Arts 4, Essence 1; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Form<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Cobra Eye Splendor, King Cobra Strikes<br /> While Cobra Form is active, the martial artist adds +2 to the duration of any poison she uses (this includes Essence Venom Strike).<br /> In addition any initiative lost due to the effects of poison is gained by the martial artist who knows how to exploit such weaknesses.<br /> Special activation rules: Cobra Form may be activated reflexively if the Exalt\u2019s opponent drops from a higher initiative to a lower initiative without the use of Withering Attacks. This is traditionally achieved through through poisons, though the Cobra isn\u2019t terribly picky.<br /> <br /> Raising the Cobra\u2019s Hood<br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Martial Arts 4, Essence 2; Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Cobra Form<br /> The Cobra Stylist targets a character who is within at least Medium Range and suffering from the effects of one of his poisons and rolls (Manipulation + Martial Arts) as a special kind grapple<br /> opposed by the target\u2019s Resolve. A grapple initiated by Raising the Cobra\u2019s Hood may only be used to Restrain/Drag the victim.<br /> If the poison's effects wear off the grapple is immediately broken.<br /> <br /> Dread Scale Fascination<br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Martial Arts 5, Essence 2; Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only, Perilous<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Cobra Form<br /> Once per scene, the Cobra Stylist may cancel out the damage of a Decisive attack at the cost of 1 health level per round of duration his poisons are reduced by.<br /> The miraculous recovery of victims who were previous succumbing to deadly venoms often provides an excellent opportunity to escape.<br /> <br /> <br /> Death Dreaming Flux<br /> Cost: 6m; Mins: Martial Arts 4, Essence 2; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords:<br /> Duration: One-Scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Cobra Form<br /> The Martial Artist may target one character under the effect of their poison calling forth visions of their worst nightmares to assail them as they succumb to the venom of the cobra.<br /> Once per scene this charm \u201ccreates\u201d a battle group with traits comparable to a Battle Group of Conscripts with Size 2, Average Drill and Might 0. This unit only exists within the target\u2019s mind and may not attack or be engaged by any other combatants and ceases to exist if they should overcome the poison.<br /> The Cobra Stylist may increase the Might of the unit if they learn of any intimacies of Fear that the target possesses by a rating equal to the intimacy level. As a final benefit he may sacrifice Initiative gained from Cobra Form to instead restore the unit\u2019s magnitude.<br /> This charm may be reset if the Cobra Stylist learns of any new intimacies of fear among those he has poisoned.<br /> <br /> Touch of Finality<br /> Cost: 4m 1wp; Mins: Martial Arts 5, Essence 3; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:<br /> Once Per Scene, The Martial Artist may hasten the inevitable with a successful Decisive Attack the duration of all poisons in the victim\u2019s bloodstream are set to 0 and they suffer the ill effects of every round at once.<br /> <br /> Marked by Eternity<br /> Cost: -(5m); Mins: Martial Arts 5, Essence 3; Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms:<br /> This charm allows the Martial Artist to store up to (Stamina) poisons in his body safely until spending 5 motes to activate them. Active poisons affect the Martial Artist normally but may be used upon others with any successful Decisive Attacks.<br /> As a final benefit the Cobra Stylist may commit 5 motes to halt the effect of any poison that he has internalised either when resisting poison or treating it in another. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 07-09-2017, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T21:46:49-07:00","id":1111977,"title":"","content":"I'll play around with it some and see if I can work with it. It'll be my second crack at homebrew mechanics for Ex3, so hopefully it won't be too terrible.<br /> <br /> I may post some questions about particular things as I'm working on it.<br /> <br /> My first thoughts is that there are a LOT of once per scene effects which locks a good portion of the style away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1333,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1333-wednesday","user":"Wednesday","date":". 07-06-2017, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1333-wednesday","name":"Wednesday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T09:40:01-07:00","id":1113773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wednesday</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1111412-cobra-style?p=1111977#post1111977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first thoughts is that there are a LOT of once per scene effects which locks a good portion of the style away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's very possible I overdid it. I'll explain my thought process on each of them and you can proceed accordingly. <br /> <br /> Showing the Cobra\u2019s Fangs- I wanted an initial &quot;you're poisoned&quot; moment for the style that was very effective at doing that without enabling the stylist to just kill someone outright and something they wouldn't just keep attempting until it worked. I was more conservative with this charm than I otherwise might have been since it predates Martial Arts being treated like separate abilities and requiring a Merit so there was a desire to avoid cherry picking here that I no longer think is necessary. The way Blinding Spark Distraction appears to be handled in 3e Dragon-Blooded, I'm wondering if a join battle roll that automatically poisons one or more people could work. <br /> <br /> Dread Scale Fascination- I was aiming to evoke video game boss where the player wins and everything goes back to normal but on the martial artist's terms. I had concerns about them constantly poisoning non-combatants to use them like ablative health levels in a manner like how you're not supposed to use Initiative. <br /> <br /> Death Dreaming Flux- Oh this one's rather simple, the book keeping on multiple hallucinatory battle groups that each fight only one person is probably more of a nightmare for the Storyteller than its victims. Also the reset condition, if this style isn't making people afraid of you something is very wrong. <br /> <br /> Touch of Finality- Being able to make people suffer the effects of multiple rounds of poisoning all at once is powerful in a way that potentially undercuts the style's theatrics. You just follow up with another decisive attack as soon as possible and end them, but the idea was that if Touch of Finality was rationed it could be something hanging over a potential poison victim struggling for their life.<br /> With the right application it will end them in a heartbeat but if they get ahead of themselves it can be wasted. <br /> <br /> Simply put, my vision of a Cobra Stylist is arrogant and assured that their poisons will do most of the work for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T01:09:26-07:00","id":1119206,"title":"","content":"So I did a bit of tooling around with it. I adjusted costs, added some Mastery keywords and added a few details or clarifications. I didn't go too ambitious because it my first tweaking of the system.<br /> <br /> It still doesn't feel done, but I wanted to post them before I forgot. Feel free to give feedback.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Showing the Cobra\u2019s Fangs<br /> Cost: 3m, Mins: Martial Arts 3, Essence 1; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only <br /> Duration: One Action<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> Once per scene, the Martial Artist may halve the halve the Hardness of his target but ignores any damage that his attack may inflict in favor of poisoning the target with Serpent\u2019s Venom.<br /> <br /> This charm is reset upon successfully crashing an opponent.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Added a reset)<br /> <br /> Cobra Eye Splendor<br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Martial Arts 3, Essence 1; Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Terrestrial<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Showing the Cobra\u2019s Fangs<br /> The Martial Artist uses his expertise with poisons and its effects upon the mind coupled with hypnotic snake-like movements dull their opponent\u2019s ability to land a blow.<br /> In response to an attack the Martial Artist may doubles any poison based penalties that the attacker is suffering from.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial: Dragon-Blooded who use this charm are limited to increasing the penalties of their opponents by up to their Essence.<br /> <br /> (Added the terrestrial keyword)<br /> <br /> King Cobra Strikes<br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Martial Arts 3, Essence 1; Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Counterattack, Decisive-only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Showing the Cobra\u2019s Fangs<br /> The Martial Artist makes an unarmed counterattack which happens after the attack roll of the opponent, but before damage is rolled. This is a decisive attack which if it succeeds at doing damage to the opponent. poisons the target with Serpent\u2019s Venom.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Just added the language from other counterattack charms)<br /> <br /> Cobra Form<br /> Cost: 6m, Mins: Martial Arts 3, Essence 1; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Form<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Cobra Eye Splendor, King Cobra Strikes<br /> While Cobra Form is active, the martial artist adds +2 to the duration of any poison she uses (this includes Essence Venom Strike).<br /> In addition any initiative lost due to poison used by the martial artist is added to their initiative, because they best know how to exploit such weakness.<br /> <br /> Special activation rules: Cobra Form may be activated reflexively if the Exalt\u2019s opponent drops from a higher initiative to a lower initiative without the use of Withering Attacks. This is traditionally achieved through poisons, though the Cobra isn\u2019t terribly picky. <br /> <br /> <br /> (Added a bit in there about poisons the Martial Artist used, as I imagined the sheer terribleness of a group of people all using poisons on a target and the Cobra stylist gobbling it all up).<br /> <br /> Raising the Cobra\u2019s Hood<br /> Cost: 4m; Mins: Martial Arts 4, Essence 2; Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Mastery<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Cobra Form<br /> The Cobra Stylist targets a character who is within Medium Range and currently suffering from the effects of one of his poisons and rolls (Manipulation + Martial Arts) as a special grapple<br /> opposed by the target\u2019s Resolve. A grapple initiated by Raising the Cobra\u2019s Hood may only be used to Restrain/Drag the victim.<br /> If the poison's effects wear off the grapple is immediately broken.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mastery: If the martial artist drags the target within close range of himself, the target will make a withering attack on the martial artist. The urge to attack may be resisted by spending 1 wp.<br /> <br /> (Added the Mastery effect based on the original and to offer an opportunity for the stylist to hit the target with a King Cobra Strike)<br /> <br /> Dread Scale Fascination<br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Martial Arts 5, Essence 2; Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only, Perilous, Mastery<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Cobra Form<br /> Once per scene, the Cobra Stylist may cancel out the damage of a Decisive attack at the cost of 1 health level per round of duration his poisons are reduced by.<br /> The miraculous recovery of victims who were previous succumbing to deadly venoms often provides an excellent opportunity to escape.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mastery: Characters who have their poison duration reduced still take the penalty as though the poison was in their system.<br /> <br /> (Added a Mastery keyword that is something similar from Snake style. I think this nicely balanced the once per scene restriction. I debated increasing the cost.)<br /> <br /> Death Dreaming Flux<br /> Cost: 8m; Mins: Martial Arts 4, Essence 2; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Mastery<br /> Duration: One-Scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Cobra Form<br /> The Martial Artist may target one character under the effect of their poison calling forth visions of their worst nightmares to assail them as they succumb to the venom of the cobra.<br /> Once per scene this charm \u201ccreates\u201d a battle group with traits comparable to a Battle Group of Conscripts with Size 2, Average Drill and Might 0. This unit only exists within the target\u2019s mind and may not attack or be engaged by any other combatants and ceases to exist if they should overcome the poison. <br /> <br /> The Cobra Stylist may increase the Might of the unit if they learn of any intimacies of Fear that the target possesses by a rating equal to the intimacy level. As a final benefit he may sacrifice Initiative gained from Cobra Form to instead restore the unit\u2019s magnitude.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mastery: Charm may be reset if the target is Crashed by their hallucinations or by poison.<br /> <br /> (Added a Mastery keyword and altered the reset. It seemed very unlikely that the Stylist would have the opportunity to learn a new intimacy in the midst of a combat scene. I could be wrong... let me know your thoughts<br /> <br /> Also, increased the cost to 8 motes, though I debated adding a wp cost instead. Still not experience with the system to be comfortable in costs on unique effects)<br /> <br /> Touch of Finality<br /> Cost: 6m 1wp; Mins: Martial Arts 5, Essence 3; Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:<br /> Once per scene, the Martial Artist may hasten the inevitable with a successful Decisive Attack, all remaining poison in the target\u2019s system strikes simultaneously. Each remaining round of duration is rolled for damage as appropriate to the poison. If poisons with initiative damage reduce the target\u2019s initiative to zero, any remaining successes are applied to the target\u2019s health track as normal. The target can only take lethal damage to the max of dice of damage for poisons which do lethal damage.<br /> <br /> (Clarified this charm mostly to avoid questions. If poisons with different effects in Crash were present, I also wanted to clarify you couldn\u2019t get more lethal damage than made sense. Raised the cost because this is a potential instant finisher.)<br /> <br /> Marked by Eternity<br /> Cost: -(5m); Mins: Martial Arts 5, Essence 3; Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Decisive-Only, Mastery<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms:<br /> This charm allows the Martial Artist to store up to (Stamina) poisons in his body safely until spending 5 motes to activate them. Active poisons affect the Martial Artist normally but may be used upon others with any successful Decisive Attacks. The martial artist can transfer as many poisons as they are storing when they make a successful decisive attack.<br /> <br /> The Cobra Stylist may commit 5 motes to halt the effect of any poison that he has internalized either when resisting poison or treating it in another.<br /> <br /> Mastery: By committing the 5 motes used to activate poisons through Marked by Eternity, any poisons transferred to a target can be halted from progressing. This causes the mark the martial artist bears to appear on the target. Releasing the commitment allows the poisons to take their normal course.<br /> <br /> (I really liked the effect from the old Cobra style of marking them and being able to hold it over the person. When the idea behind the Martial Artist of the new style as described, I felt it fit them too.)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1333-wednesday","name":"Wednesday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T14:35:35-07:00","id":1119631,"title":"","content":"Not bad at all some very logical additions and I actually really like what you did with the Mastery for Marked by Eternity.<br /> <br /> One nitpick, though that may have been me trying to be too clever with the original charm in the first place.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wednesday</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1111412-cobra-style?p=1119206#post1119206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Added a Mastery keyword and altered the reset. It seemed very unlikely that the Stylist would have the opportunity to learn a new intimacy in the midst of a combat scene. I could be wrong... let me know your thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The primary intent was that a Cobra Stylist would be incentivised to use Threatern actions to create new intimacies of Fear. It's a very theatrical style that preys upon people's distorted reality and also has this unfair (and rather meta) advantage that if the martial artist is defeated too abruptly then their victims will lose the cusion of Initiative they get from being in combat and the poison's remaining duration will attack their health levels directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T10:48:06-07:00","id":1119950,"title":"","content":"Um, minor question: What are Cobra Styles form weapons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T10:56:20-07:00","id":1119954,"title":"","content":"This is off-topic, but I'm always amused that we have both Snake Style and Cobra Style. We shouldn't stop there, we should make <i>Equatorial Spitting Cobra Style</i>, and eventually Fred, The Equatorial Spitting Cobra Style.<br /> <br /> Then we can go in the other direction and make <i>Scaled Reptile Style</i> and <i>Reptile Style</i> and <i>Animal Style</i> and <i>Living Thing Style</i> and just <i>Thing Style.</i><br /> <br /> (Actually, I guess <i>Thing Style</i> is basic enough to be <i>Beige Existence of Nondescript Things</i>, the style for the set of objects that have no properties other than being in this set.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T11:38:44-07:00","id":1119971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1111412-cobra-style?p=1119954#post1119954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is off-topic, but I'm always amused that we have both Snake Style and Cobra Style. We shouldn't stop there, we should make <i>Equatorial Spitting Cobra Style</i>, and eventually Fred, The Equatorial Spitting Cobra Style.<br /> <br /> Then we can go in the other direction and make <i>Scaled Reptile Style</i> and <i>Reptile Style</i> and <i>Animal Style</i> and <i>Living Thing Style</i> and just <i>Thing Style.</i><br /> <br /> (Actually, I guess <i>Thing Style</i> is basic enough to be <i>Beige Existence of Nondescript Things</i>, the style for the set of objects that have no properties other than being in this set.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I... just realized that this concept kind of applies to the old Terrestrial/Celestial/Sidereal divide design. Terrestrial styles were often named after pretty niche specific <i>things</i>, while Celestial were broader categories, and Sidereal were super broad unspecific concepts. Neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T15:11:28-07:00","id":1120095,"title":"","content":"Also the idea that Snake Style as a Celestial Martial Art is some metaphysically correct way to emulate a snake that makes someone naming a different style after a specific type of snake absurd.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1111412-cobra-style?p=1119950#post1119950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, minor question: What are Cobra Styles form weapons?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was still going with paired swords as per Ink Monkeys Vol 39.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T19:50:47-07:00","id":1120594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1111412-cobra-style?p=1119631#post1119631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The primary intent was that a Cobra Stylist would be incentivised to use Threatern actions to create new intimacies of Fear. It's a very theatrical style that preys upon people's distorted reality and also has this unfair (and rather meta) advantage that if the martial artist is defeated too abruptly then their victims will lose the cusion of Initiative they get from being in combat and the poison's remaining duration will attack their health levels directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a pretty cheeky &quot;back-up&quot; in there. I'll admit I hadn't thought about giving them a fear-based intimacy during combat. I can see what you are going for there.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the commentary. Did the changes in cost make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1333-wednesday","name":"Wednesday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T12:50:12-07:00","id":1124897,"title":"","content":"Sorry I thought I'd replied to this.<br /> I felt that the cost changes made sense, it's really one of those things that's going to need some wiggle room until there's an opertunity for playtesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T21:37:47-07:00","id":1126170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1111412-cobra-style?p=1119954#post1119954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is off-topic, but I'm always amused that we have both Snake Style and Cobra Style. We shouldn't stop there, we should make <i>Equatorial Spitting Cobra Style</i>, and eventually Fred, The Equatorial Spitting Cobra Style.<br /> <br /> Then we can go in the other direction and make <i>Scaled Reptile Style</i> and <i>Reptile Style</i> and <i>Animal Style</i> and <i>Living Thing Style</i> and just <i>Thing Style.</i><br /> <br /> (Actually, I guess <i>Thing Style</i> is basic enough to be <i>Beige Existence of Nondescript Things</i>, the style for the set of objects that have no properties other than being in this set.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Animal Style would be the Terrible Ascent-Driven Beast, which has the note that some barbarian tribes call it the Paragon of Animals and possibly consider it as combining aspects of multiple animals rather than attempting to emulate a single predator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3353-rca","name":"RCa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T11:42:15-07:00","id":1208085,"title":"","content":"I'm going to have to update this style in light of the clarification that poison doesn't penalise static values since a big point of the visuals I had in mind were<br /> &quot;I've poisoned you, you're seeing double which one am I?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}